---
/**
 * THE CLOSING STATEMENT — a SHARED component (R36 item 7, Oscar
 * 2026-09-04): the fragmented statement section + the red tail,
 * extracted VERBATIM from LandingClosing.astro (frame 13:277's
 * composition, the dline grammar) so the landing and /services carry
 * one instance each of the same section. Driven by
 * closing-statement.js (dwell, white → red scrub, nav-over-red,
 * entrance); styled by landing.css (.landing-closing-st*,
 * .landing-closing-tail — page-agnostic under .landing-v2). Desktop
 * only (display:none ≤1024 on both pages).
 *
 * COPY: the same lines on both pages — on /services this is a
 * PLACEHOLDER pending Oscar's services-specific statement (flagged).
 */
/* ── FRAGMENTED STATEMENT (frame 13:277, x88 y1264, 1616×727) — the
   We Create Access dline grammar verbatim: Dazzed Bold 100/88/−4%
   UPPERCASE ink, absolutely positioned lines, authored x/y (the
   pitch is deliberately irregular: 90/88/101/90...). Supersedes the
   old right-hand intro paragraph on desktop (mobile keeps its own).
   Line 3's wide word-gap is AUTHORED SPACES (white-space: pre). */
const ST_LINES = [
  { x: 374, y: 0, t: 'The' },
  { x: 295, y: 90, t: 'network effect' },
  { x: 88, y: 178, t: 'exists            to connect people,' },
  { x: 565, y: 279, t: 'brands and talent' },
  { x: 201, y: 369, t: 'in ways that create' },
  { x: 228, y: 459, t: 'long-term' },
  { x: 1037, y: 459, t: 'cultural' },
  { x: 410, y: 549, t: 'and commercial' },
  { x: 1007, y: 639, t: 'value.' },
];
/* ── THE PHONE'S FOURTEEN LINES (frame 1:373 at 402, applied
   2026-09-09): the same statement re-broken as the frame draws it —
   fourteen single-word (or two-word) fragments on a 45 pitch at 48,
   each at an authored x (`x`, from the page's left edge) or flush to
   an authored RIGHT edge (`r`, likewise). The frame's "NETWORK" box at
   x14 is read as the 16 margin (a 2px slip). Rendered hidden at every
   width and shown only below 768 (shared-narrow.css), so the desktop's
   nine lines and their dwell, entrance and ink centring are untouched;
   the phone's dwell measures this block instead. "exists" is authored
   lowercase in the frame under an uppercase style — it renders caps,
   as the desktop's line does. */
const ST_LINES_M = [
  { x: 82, t: 'The' },
  { x: 16, t: 'network' },
  { r: 386, t: 'effect exists' },
  { r: 386, t: 'to connect' },
  { x: 155, t: 'people,' },
  { x: 16, t: 'brands and' },
  { x: 63, t: 'talent' },
  { r: 386, t: 'in ways that' },
  { x: 201, t: 'create' },
  { x: 79, t: 'long-term' },
  { x: 16, t: 'cultural' },
  { x: 40, t: 'and' },
  { x: 16, t: 'commercial' },
  { r: 354, t: 'value.' },
];
---

{/* ── THE FRAGMENTED STATEMENT — its own full-width flow section
    (desktop only; ≤1024 keeps the shipped mobile closing untouched).
    The 54px breathing space to the closing above lives INSIDE the
    section (+54 on every line top) so the box sits flush against the
    closing — a margin here was a transparent strip that exposed the
    fixed hero video. The read gap from the descriptions stays the
    frame's 225. */}
<section class="landing-closing-st" data-closing-st aria-label="The network effect">
  {/* The DWELL stage (Oscar R3, 2026-08-26): sticky slack — the
      closing's own hold mechanism reused. The stage pins when the
      statement's centre crosses the viewport centre (sticky top =
      50dvh − half the stage) and holds for the section's extra
      --closing-st-hold of scroll. Pure CSS: scrub-native,
      reversible, and the RM static equivalent for free. */}
  <div class="landing-closing-st__stage" data-closing-st-stage>
    {ST_LINES.map((l) => (
      <p class="landing-closing-st__line" data-closing-st-line style={`left:${l.x}px;top:${l.y + 54}px`}>{l.t}</p>
    ))}
    {/* the phone's fourteen lines (1:373) — hidden above 767; the
        driver reveals whichever set is rendered. The full stop on
        "value." stays with the desktop's shared copy (the frame draws
        none — read as a slip, like WE BUILD's colon). */}
    {ST_LINES_M.map((l) => (
      <p
        class={`landing-closing-st__mline${l.r ? ' landing-closing-st__mline--r' : ''}`}
        data-closing-st-mline
        style={l.r ? `--st-r:${386 - l.r}` : `--st-x:${l.x - 16}`}
      >{l.t}</p>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

{/* THE RED TAIL — R21 (Oscar 2026-09-02): 180px of the final red
    ground below the statement section (was the 500 exit-fade tail of
    R16). The sequence is now white arrival → white→red while the
    text is fixed (R23: over 600 of scroll, half speed) → the footer
    revealed from beneath this tail's bottom edge; the tail fades
    WITH the section during the dwell (landing-closing.js) and stays
    red. R23: the statement section ends at "value."'s ink bottom, so
    this 180 is THE gap from that ink to the reveal. Desktop only
    (display:none ≤1024, like the statement section). z260: the
    closing tier over the footer (259). */}
<div class="landing-closing-tail" data-closing-tail aria-hidden="true"></div>
